\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Graph families and pool sizes. Deterministic families are split by $n \bmod  3$ (grids by shape index $\bmod  3$). The residue class not shown is reserved for a separate development pool. Random families are drawn from independent seeds and resampled until non-isomorphic to every catalogue graph and to the other pools. Counts are derived from the evaluator's catalogue and plane configuration.}}{5}{table.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:roster}{{1}{5}{Graph families and pool sizes. Deterministic families are split by $n \bmod 3$ (grids by shape index $\bmod 3$). The residue class not shown is reserved for a separate development pool. Random families are drawn from independent seeds and resampled until non-isomorphic to every catalogue graph and to the other pools. Counts are derived from the evaluator's catalogue and plane configuration}{table.caption.6}{}}
