\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Per-family reliability map on held-out graphs; families are sorted by the best bound's error (bound slack), increasing upward. (a) Mean absolute log error of our predictor (circles) and of the best bound (squares, log scale). The best-bound error per family is derived as our predictor's error minus the paired difference. (b) Paired difference in error (our predictor minus best bound) with 95\% two-level bootstrap CI. Blue intervals exclude zero; the grey lollipop interval includes zero.}}{7}{figure.caption.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:family}{{3}{7}{Per-family reliability map on held-out graphs; families are sorted by the best bound's error (bound slack), increasing upward. (a) Mean absolute log error of our predictor (circles) and of the best bound (squares, log scale). The best-bound error per family is derived as our predictor's error minus the paired difference. (b) Paired difference in error (our predictor minus best bound) with 95\% two-level bootstrap CI. Blue intervals exclude zero; the grey lollipop interval includes zero}{figure.caption.13}{}}
